WEBVTT

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.190
It's so strange,

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.150
to think there's a part of space
with hardly any stars in sight.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.360
It's been like this for a while now.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.150
It's very quiet.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.120
Oh, no!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:16.990
What's wrong?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.990
We left the club room the way it was.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.580
What will happen to it?

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.790
Good question...

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.620
Who knows what'll happen?

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:25.580
Next!

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.090
The fragment stopped accelerating!

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.720
The next jump should be our last.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:38.010
At the Water's Edge

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.770
Subaru, you can see it, right?

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.060
Yeah, I can. The last fragment.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.520
We're going to capture it.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.480
However, it's hard to imagine

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.280
the fragment will just be waiting
there for us after we jump.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.660
I can't even guess what will
happen once we reach it.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.910
But we still have to go!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.460
She's right. We're so close.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.330
You agree, don't you, Nanako?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.630
Correct.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.800
Very well. Let's go!

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.510
What's that? Space is twisted?

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.890
It's a gravitational lens!

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.180
A phenomenon caused when strong gravitation

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.640
creates spatial distortions that bend light.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.900
Most likely, that's a singularity!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.270
What's that?

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.030
Energy gathers at a single point,
and when it exceeds its limit,

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:38.070
it collapses along with space-time itself,
faster than the speed of light.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.660
That's a singularity.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.160
It's a black hole!

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.410
Is it a point or a hole? Make up your mind!

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.460
But the fragment is...

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.540
Yeah, it's there.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.920
I guess it really is impossible for us to gather
all the fragments in this universe.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.590
You're saying that again?

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.300
That we don't want to finish
collecting the fragments?

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:58.180
Huh?

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.930
Don't worry. It's not just you.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.680
We all decided

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.060
that we're not going to give up!

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.140
Aoi...

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:13.150
It's unusual to see such a distinct
Schwarzschild event horizon.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.940
That's a black hole?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.860
Yes, it's the universe's horizon plane,
like the horizon line on Earth.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.450
What lies beyond is completely
cut off from this universe.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.740
But the fragment is inside it, right?

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.790
We exceeded the speed of
light to get here, too.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.830
We've only moved within this universe.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.420
However, the final fragment is trying
to escape from this universe itself.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.300
Everyone, take these!

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.600
Whoa...

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:52.060
Use these fragments to draw the final
fragment out of the black hole!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.570
Draw the fragment with other fragments?

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.190
I shall try it.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.330
I'll try it, too.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.210
All right, now I'll try!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.670
President?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.930
I guess I don't have power like you all do...

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.140
If we just had one more...

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.800
There's no way!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.690
<i>If the final fragment is here, then...</i>

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.270
Subaru?

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.900
Minato!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.900
Him?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.120
I'll bring him here!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.780
Subaru!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.580
Minato, help us!

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.380
We need your power, Minato!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.800
Help you?

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.170
I haven't given up on my own goal.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.340
What are you planning to do
without a single fragment?

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.600
At that rate, you'll just fall in!

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.850
If I'm swallowed by a black hole
and erased from this universe,

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.100
that wouldn't be so bad.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:18.230
Me and the "stars" that couldn't
become anything, just like me...

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.530
No! I won't let you do that!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.940
H-Huh?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.070
Hey! What are you doing?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.620
I'm sorry—

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.830
Stop it!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.090
No!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.840
I wonder if Subaru's all right.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.180
Subaru's planning to make
him our sixth member.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.970
Huh?! But he betrayed Subaru!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.850
Subaru... You wouldn't understand.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.230
All these "stars" that never
amounted to anything...

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.980
You'll never understand how we feel,
being denied any chance at all.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.280
I don't understand.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.740
How could I understand that?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:13.250
I just don't want the warmth I feel
from you right now to disappear.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.460
I don't want the kindness and sadness within you

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.750
to be erased, like it was never there!

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.460
No matter how many times
we redo the universe,

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:26.380
there was only one Minato I met.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.720
Subaru...

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:31.720
You saw it, right?

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:37.100
My real self might not even
be able to speak to you...

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.360
But we still met each other.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.230
And since we met, I don't want to forget you.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.400
I can't pretend you never existed!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.490
I...

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.740
Tell me how you really feel, Minato!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.210
I never actually said out loud what I wanted,

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:05.380
or that I wanted to be with anyone, did I?

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.380
Then I'll say it!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.390
I want to be with you, Minato!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.640
I'll be the one to make you happy!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.020
You can't do—

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.480
I will!

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.100
I'll do it right now!

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.770
She's coming back!

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.950
Oh, my goodness!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.120
Hey!

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.910
It's huge! What is it this time?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.000
It's our spaceship!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.250
I called it here!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.250
What? What?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.880
But I thought it was broken.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.220
It's still broken.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.260
But if we miss this opportunity,
it will all be for naught.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.050
This is the spaceship...

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.140
You recognize it?

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.890
Then he's making his move, as well...

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.320
Everyone!

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.910
Huh? Wait, did you guys see that?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.000
I-It's not what you... W-Well, it is, but, um...

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.120
Let's hurry.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:21.920
Huh?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.630
You need me to go with you, right?

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:28.920
Yes!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.430
I understand. All right.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.970
I'll have faith in Subaru,
and entrust the fragments to you.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.070
Wh-What?

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:50.030
How did you end up looking like a mollusk?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.700
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.570
Why don't you just remember already?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.330
I'm your Aldebaran.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.590
Huh? I'm...

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:10.550
The president turned into a human!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.970
And I kind of sat on him the other day...

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.140
You're Elnath.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.970
My one and only friend,
whom I met seven years ago.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.980
Minato? You're Minato?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.440
But you're awfully different
from the Minato I knew...

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.990
I guess your time had stopped
since that moment...

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.490
I... I can't breathe!

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.370
I'm sorry.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.500
Everyone! Are you ready?

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.380
An eye for an eye,

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.630
a tooth for a tooth!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.510
The only thing that can counter a
black hole is another black hole!

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.180
Right now, the fragments placed in six locations

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.810
on the spaceship are synchronized
with your drive shafts.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.310
Once you hit the accelerator,
they'll use vacuum energy

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.230
to create new singularities.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.020
In other words, we'll use the
power of six black holes

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:16.200
to draw the remaining fragment out of that
black hole, back into this universe.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:26.290
This spaceship will support our
black holes, so give it your all!

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.340
It started glowing!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.550
It's Hawking radiation.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.300
It's forcing the black hole's energy
back into the vacuum of space.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.550
Now turn it inside-out!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:56.950
What's that sound?

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.950
It's the groaning of the ship under
the black holes' opposing pulls!

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.450
We have no options left...
We'll just have to see this through.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.210
If we either do it or we don't,
then let's do it to the end!

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:12.460
It was fun being a magic user,
but that's our decision!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.840
Let us obtain the last fragment together.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.470
We'll see it through to the end!

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.140
The space around us is collapsing from the strain.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:25.470
It'll swallow us!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.190
No! Don't give up!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.960
Where are we?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:55.920
It's very quiet.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.880
We passed through the black hole.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.180
Then we didn't make it in time?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.010
No, just before we fell into the black hole,

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:08.180
we barely managed to grab the fragment,
and revived our engine.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.270
The spaceship's fixed?

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:14.060
Yes. Allow me to thank you on
behalf of all my comrades.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.030
Thank you, everyone.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.030
Where do you plan to go?

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:24.030
You possess the power to control probability,
but you rejected the act of choice.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.870
Weren't you only delaying your own demises?

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:30.160
You're certainly right.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.210
However, that's only true in your universe.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.420
In ours?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.630
Look there!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.840
That's our next destination, the next universe.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:45.850
You mean you were traversing universes?

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.470
Even if it's not possible in your universe,

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.350
another potential might
exist in another universe.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.060
That's what we placed our hopes on.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.230
Your hopes...

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.650
Yes. As long as we have hope,

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:01.240
we can continue our journey,
crossing even whole universes.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.030
Are you surprised?

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:10.000
I cursed myself by looking only at the past,
and got your people involved.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.920
That's all in the past now.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.000
Oh, right! We'll take our shiny lights, too.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.760
There certainly are fewer now, huh?

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.010
What are those?

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.390
Crystallized potentials that once resided
in human hearts, but were expelled.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.850
And this, as well...

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.070
This...

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:42.700
It's a potential life that was
never born into this world.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.240
That's...

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.330
Minato, you were trying to save them?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.370
I'll carry on Minato's goal.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.830
In a new universe, there may be a
future in which they can shine.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.710
Now, it's sad to say goodbye,
but it's time for us to leave.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:00.920
He spoke!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.380
We need to unravel the tangled
threads of your destinies, too.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:11.640
Thanks to you, we can now set off on
our journey to find new potentials.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:16.520
You all went beyond this universe's laws
to gather all the engine fragments.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.690
That's true magic.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.440
We'll be able to go home now, right?

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.610
Of course.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.570
I'd also like to do a little something to thank you.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.910
Could you help me?

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.030
Yeah, let's do it.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:35.620
No matter what shape I take,
I'll always be your Pleiadian.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.280
Well, we should go, too.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:05.650
Go where?

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.740
A new spaceship?

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:13.910
This is the shape of the destinies
of all the lives born on Earth.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.950
I don't get it!

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.080
Just as a single string may play various notes,

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.920
this is one possible shape of our universe.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.420
You mean the threads of the destinies
we were in before are in this, too?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.420
You see, when I looked up

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:32.430
everyone was smiling at me

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:32.430
Yes, we're also a part of this vast potential.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:41.940
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.430
It suddenly grows thicker and thinner in places.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.480
Right there, it ends partway.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.690
The branches decrease.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.940
We're heading toward the past?

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:51.450
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.940
Though the threads of destiny branch infinitely,

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.700
as you follow them into the past,
they eventually converge on a single point.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:48.780
...my daily life...

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.990
Is that our destination?

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:51.450
Yes.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:15:01.170
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.450
The source of all potentials.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:03.040
"Can I fly?"

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.420
It's an ocean!

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:03.750
Look at that!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:07.260
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.960
What's that? The Moon?

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.630
They say that, long ago,
the Moon appeared larger

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:12.890
We can go there whenever we want to

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.760
because it orbited closer to Earth.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:16.470
Here, the very first potential has yet to be born.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:22.560
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:21.270
The giant Moon covers the sky,
and the oceans have only just formed.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.730
It's still a primitive planet,
without a single fragment of life.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.190
"We have to catch them!"

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.990
This is Earth was four billion years ago,
back when it was still nothing.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:31.700
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:35.370
That's why the potential for all kinds
of life exists right here, right now.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:37.490
the scenery around us glittered

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:39.750
From here, we can choose however
we want to live our lives anew.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:42.170
sometime after school

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.170
We can become anything.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.250
We can start over from any point.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:45.290
Huh?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.750
Start over anywhere?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:51.510
This is the gift granted to you
by the ones who just departed.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.050
Now, what will you all choose?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:57.760
You see, there's a reason you get born

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:57.760
I...

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:03.270
Nobody knows what it is

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.390
I...

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.020
I...

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:02.640
I...

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.480
The idea of infinite potential is
so vast, I don't even know.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:12.570
But people still keep searching for a spell to prove their existence

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:10.320
All I can imagine is a girl who
isn't too different from me.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:13.410
An ordinary, everyday girl.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:21.500
Days with too much freedom might be too much to handle for some

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.530
I wish I were smarter, like Hikaru.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.910
...freedom...

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:20.330
I wish my hair were prettier, like Itsuki's.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:24.330
I wish I could take things at my
own pace, like Nanako.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:31.550
So they keep looking for the very thing to do

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.170
I wish I were more together, like Aoi.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:32.590
I wish I could be more direct
and honest, like Subaru.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:32.590
"It'll be fine!"

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:37.970
I'm sure the reason we envy each other is
because we've all helped each other a lot

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:36.970
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:43.020
If you can't wait, let's go right away

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.060
when we were in trouble or feeling down.

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.560
It wasn't that we wanted to
become some perfect person.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:52.690
Each star sticker you stick on will speed you up

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.060
It was because everyone was themselves.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.570
And because I was myself.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.320
And because of the time we were able to share.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.320
In that case, I want to be me.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:57.320
"I want to embrace you!"

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.570
And I want to help find lots of good

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:00.830
and beautiful aspects of the
people I'm with at the time.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:01.830
Of course you'll make it

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.670
I will be me.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:07.830
because the promise between us

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:11.840
is for all eternity after school

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.960
It appears you've decided.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.840
Hey...

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:13.720
What are you going to do?

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:19.720
There isn't much time left.
Just worry about yourselves.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.980
Uh, so, well...

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:28.270
What should we say at a time like this?

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.900
I'm sure we'll be all right.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.280
Even if I go back to being me,

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.940
it will be the me that changed
after meeting all of you.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:37.160
I have faith, too. In myself and all of you.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:41.990
Danke. Grazie. Merci. Xie xie. Thank you.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.750
I love you all!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.500
Me, too.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.500
Don't cry, Subaru!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.250
Do you think we were able to change?

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.300
Absolutely.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.510
What does that mean?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.260
I'm sure we have.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:58.800
Yeah.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.650
It's still warm...

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.080
Everyone, take care.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.700
Adieu...

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.340
Well, shall we go, too?

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:37.840
Huh?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.590
You and I are going together, Minato.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.430
I'm only a guide...

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.350
My role is already over.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.640
I promised, remember?

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.770
That I would make you happy.

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:55.650
But in your world, my potential is...

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.280
We're still going.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:07.620
I wonder how long four billion years will take.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.790
Not very long. Just a brief nap.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.800
What should I do? I'm a little bit scared.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.300
Don't worry. I'll stay by your side the whole time.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:23.510
I'll stay awake the whole time, too.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.810
This time, let's go see the stars together...

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:31.850
You tell me I have to live...

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.730
There's no end to how cruel you are.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.300
It's already this late?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.300
Oh, you're going now?

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:03.220
Yeah, there's a meteor shower tonight.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.050
That's right...

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:07.260
All right, I'll walk you out.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:08.970
If you want, I could go with y—

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.430
Hey.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:11.890
O-Oh...

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.190
See you later!

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:20.030
Subaru's in middle school now.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:20.900
That's right.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.410
She won't stay a child forever.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:34.540
Aoi...

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.760
Suba—

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.760
Aoi—

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:45.760
Why—

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:45.760
Hey—

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.810
It's been a while.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:52.270
I've seen you around at this
hour from time to time.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:59.570
Hey, I always thought I should tell you...

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:04.570
I took the exam for this school
because I wanted to wear this uniform.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.530
But I was so embarrassed
by that reason,

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:10.410
I just couldn't tell you...

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.950
I'm sorry!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:15.460
It's okay. It was your decision.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.460
That uniform's cute.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.460
Thank you...

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.180
Is that a telescope?

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:27.800
Oh, yeah. You see, tonight...

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:28.970
Aoi!

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:30.560
Who's that?

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.720
My friend.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:34.640
I'm Subaru. Hello.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:38.270
Oh, right. Take this, if you'd like.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:36.810
Let's see the Perseids
in fall!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:37.560
Astronomers Association

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.480
Oh, sure...

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:41.780
A meteor shower?

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:45.490
Do you think we could watch
the stars together again?

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.320
Sure.

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.680
J-Jeez, why?

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:17.190
Here you go.

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:22.480
Thank you...

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:24.320
Here. Are you all right?

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:25.440
Here's one.

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:27.070
Thank you.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:28.660
Here.

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:29.320
You dropped this.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:34.240
You're in Class 1, right?

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:36.410
Oh, yeah. I'm Subaru.

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:38.370
When is the meteor shower?

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:39.500
Tonight.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:40.420
Oh?

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:41.840
Sounds interesting.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:45.090
Um, if you'd like, we could go together.

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:48.340
Astronomers Association

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:48.340
Let's see the Perseids\h
in fall!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:52.510
A meteor shower, huh?

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:59.940
<i>The stars in the night sky spend
a long time passing each other by,</i>

00:22:59.940 --> 00:23:05.530
<i>repeating the sadness of being alone
and the joy of meeting one another.</i>

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:08.150
<i>Today's forecast is a meteor shower.</i>

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:10.660
<i>When I look up at the starry sky,</i>

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:17.080
<i>it makes me think of the people I
still have yet to meet, somewhere.</i>

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:22.960
<i>That someone is looking up at the
starry sky in the same way...</i>

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:29.340
<i>And the stars are watching over
all of us from up in the sky.</i>

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:35.010
The End

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:35.010
<i>Wait for me!</i>
